      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can provide general information. Dizziness when standing up is a common side effect of Lisinopril, but it's usually temporary. Taking a double dose to \"adjust\" might not be necessary, as your body will likely adapt to the medication over time. In fact, doubling the dose can increase the risk of dizziness and other adverse effects, so it's best to consult your doctor or pharmacist for guidance.",
